      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Paint is a liquid pigment that, after applied to a solid material and allowed to dry, adds a film-like layer, usually to create an image. It can be made in many colors and types, most commonly oil-based or water-based. Primitive forms of paint were used in cave paintings. Paint serves as protection, not just color in a tin or a tube. The process of making paint involves three main ingredients: pigment, binder, and solvent.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "油漆是一种液体颜料，涂在固体材料上并允许干燥后，会添加一层薄膜，通常用来创造图像。它可以制成许多颜色和类型，最常见的是油基或水基。油漆的原始形式被用于洞穴绘画。油漆不仅仅是罐头或管子里的颜色，它还起到保护作用。制作油漆的过程涉及三个主要成分：颜料，粘合剂和溶剂。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
